{
  "id": "25th-next-generation-world-hobby-fair",
  "name": "25th Next Generation World Hobby Fair",
  "category": "event",
  "description": {
    "text": "The 25th Next Generation World Hobby Fair, the Shogakukan group's touring toy and video game fair, visited Osaka on 14 January, Tokyo on 20 and 21 January, Nagoya on 28 January and Fukuoka on 4 February 2007. At its Trade Please DP corner (とりかえっこDP), visitors swapped one Pokémon card of their own, even an old yellow-bordered card or one with the old card back, for one of eight new promos, 017 to 024/DP-P, without choosing which, while stocks lasted. Official gym events ran the same corner that January and February, and the eight came back at the Gym Challenge tournaments held to launch Secret of the Lakes.\n\nThe fair also gave out two cosmos holo special Energy cards, Darkness and Metal, both drawn by Takumi Akabane.",
